@title Cabinet: a plan made before rails ran through the device middles lists its devices as off the rail's middle
@area Cabinet
@sizes 1366x768
# qa/fixtures/door-cutouts.novo was made before rails ran through the middle of their devices, so its devices sit on the rail's line by their top edge. The Cabinet view puts a triangle on each of them; its popover and the Inspector say it for the device. The example project (rails through the middles) shows none of this.
open qa/fixtures/door-cutouts.novo
wait 20
click_text Cabinet #1
wait 30
shot old-plan
click_text "Warning: " Button
wait 10
expect "off the middle of its DIN rail"
expect "Centre rails on devices"
shot problems-named
check_layout
key Escape
wait 3
click 627 190
wait 10
scroll 1190 500 -900
wait 5
expect "off the middle of its DIN rail"
shot inspector-line
check_layout
key ctrl+k
wait 3
text issues
wait 4
key Enter
wait 10
expect "off the middle of its DIN rail"
shot check-list-row
